# Optional transfers (`T | false`)

When a value can be either a **real transfer object** or **this action did not happen**, use `Type | false` — not `null`, not `undefined`, and not a fake zero-amount object.

## Why

- Call sites read as `if (receipt.pickup)` / `pickup === false`.
- Idle stops stay honest: a pickup-only stop has `delivery: false`, not `{ before, amount: 0, after }`.
- Pickup and delivery share one transfer shape so both circumstances stay symmetric.

## Transfer shape (load / unload)

```ts
type ScuTransfer = {
  before: number; // aboard when this transfer starts
  amount: number; // SCU moved in this transfer
  after: number;  // aboard when this transfer ends
};

type StopTransferLedger = {
  pickup: ScuTransfer | false;
  delivery: ScuTransfer | false;
};
```

Canonical implementation: `lib/missions/cargoInventory.ts` (`cargoInventory.transferLedgerByStop`, `cargoInventory.peakScuAtStop`).

## Examples

```ts
// ✅ Pickup only
{ pickup: { before: 0, amount: 16, after: 16 }, delivery: false }

// ✅ Delivery only
{ pickup: false, delivery: { before: 16, amount: 16, after: 0 } }

// ✅ Both — pickup then delivery (later.before === earlier.after)
{
 pickup: { before: 10, amount: 20, after: 30 },
 delivery: { before: 30, amount: 10, after: 20 },
}

// ✅ Both — delivery then pickup (unload-then-load hub; same chaining rule)
{
 delivery: { before: 323, amount: 323, after: 0 },
 pickup: { before: 0, amount: 412, after: 412 },
}

// ❌ Zero stub for an idle transfer
{ pickup: { before: 0, amount: 16, after: 16 }, delivery: { before: 16, amount: 0, after: 16 } }

// ❌ Prefer false over null for “did not happen”
{ pickup: { before: 0, amount: 16, after: 16 }, delivery: null }
```

## When adding similar APIs

1. Define one shared object type for the active case (`ScuTransfer`, etc.).
2. Type each optional sibling as `ThatType | false`.
3. Emit `false` when amount / action is absent; emit the object only when something actually runs.
4. Narrow before use (`if (transfer)`, or pass `transfer` into UI after a truthy guard).
5. Peak / aggregate helpers must handle `false` (see `cargoInventory.peakScuAtStop`) — do not assume `pickup.after` always exists.
